const meanings={
 'lesson:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth':'Navigation container for ticket-based authentication, application authorization and enterprise AAA. All nine selected children qualify as bounded drafts; its three sections retain their current optional enrichment labels.',
 'keywords:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth':'Four bounded vocabulary entries identify ticket-based Kerberos, network-access RADIUS, administrative TACACS+ and the separate authentication/authorization/accounting functions of AAA.',
 'traps:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth':'KDC includes AS/TGS rather than the destination application. Tickets do not grant all resource access, and AAA participation does not make RADIUS/TACACS+ interchangeable.',
 'check:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth':'Given an existing valid TGT, obtaining a service ticket from TGS for the target principal is the next ticket-flow concept. This is a reveal, not a graded protocol execution.',
 'section:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth:0':'AS/TGT then TGS/service-ticket then a fresh service authenticator form the bounded ticket-flow overview. AS/TGS are logical KDC functions; the application server is separate and reusable passwords are not sent to each service.',
 'section:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth:1':'Authenticated identity/session keys differ from resource authorization, including when tickets carry policy-related information. Stolen ticket material needs associated session keys; clock validation and replay detection work together with configurable skew.',
 'section:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth:2':'RADIUS network admission and TACACS+ device administration are common uses with separate protected-path concerns. LDAP queries/binds and TLS/SASL authentication layers differ from ticket issuance; unprotected simple-bind credentials are unsafe.',
 'lesson:ot-iot-cyber-physical':'Partial navigation container for physical-process scope, safe changes, segmentation/remote access and device lifecycle. Two ambiguous generated vocabulary checks remain held; accurate sections do not rewrite them.',
 'keywords:ot-iot-cyber-physical':'Three short entries are accurate bounded vocabulary: industrial monitoring/control, supervisory data gathering and an approved maintained configuration. They do not supply exclusive ICS-versus-SCADA category discrimination.',
 'traps:ot-iot-cyber-physical':'SCADA is not every OT device; active scans/patches require engineering coordination; an air-gap label does not prove isolation across media, radios or vendor paths.',
 'check:ot-iot-cyber-physical':'A fragile production controller calls for documented risk, tested interim exposure restrictions and engineering/vendor planning for safe maintenance; no immediate disruptive patching or indefinite exception is implied. Ungraded reveal only.',
 'section:ot-iot-cyber-physical:0':'OT includes physical monitoring/change systems; ICS is industrial control within OT. SCADA supervises distributed sites, DCS distributes local process control, PLC executes field logic, and IoT provides connected sensing/processing/communications.',
 'section:ot-iot-cyber-physical:1':'Timing, availability, lifecycle/vendor constraints and physical consequences require representative testing, approved windows, engineering/process-safety ownership and rollback planning. Delayed patches need time-limited risk treatment and exposure reduction.',
 'section:ot-iot-cyber-physical:2':'Risk-based zones/conduits and required protocols combine with authenticated approved logged remote administration and removal of unused vendor access. Passive/protocol-aware monitoring, process context, safe time synchronization, backups and rehearsed fail-safe/manual operations are conditional controls.',
 'section:ot-iot-cyber-physical:3':'Procurement requires identity/default/update/support/data/logging capabilities and an end-of-support path. Inventory and constrained-device gateway/network controls support lifecycle management; disposal removes credentials/data/trust and verifies risk-appropriate sanitization or destruction.'
};
const commonLimits=['Observed objective unions and optional-enrichment labels are not precise child scope, calibrated difficulty or owner approval.','No canonical roles, trusted revisions, independent assessment family, learner evidence, verified recovery, publication or activation.'];
const limits={
 'section:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth:0':['The simplified overview does not enumerate every AS/TGS message, preauthentication variant, encryption type or authenticator exchange. Possessing a TGT alone without usable keys does not complete the protocol.','Ticket lifetimes, renewability, forwarding/proxy/constrained delegation and cross-realm policy are not taught as a complete procedure here. SSO does not grant delegation or arbitrary service access.'],
 'section:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth:1':['Clock synchronization alone does not prevent replay within the permitted skew. The source explicitly also requires replay detection; no universal hard-coded five-minute configuration is inferred.','Tickets may carry authorization data, but the service still enforces resource policy. Initial MFA does not neutralize stolen session material. Accounting/logging is a separate AAA function, not automatically supplied by every service ticket.'],
 'section:kerberos-aaa-enterprise-auth:2':['Classic RADIUS is not whole-packet confidentiality. TACACS+ legacy body obfuscation is not modern integrity/privacy/replay protection; protecting its packet path matters beyond its visible header. No protocol is declared intrinsically safe or interchangeable.','LDAP is a directory protocol; LDAPS/TLS protects transport, while SASL mechanisms differ and may or may not supply an appropriate security layer. Simple bind protection requires actual negotiated confidentiality. No port, certificate, deployment or directory authorization is verified.'],
 'keywords:ot-iot-cyber-physical':['SCADA is an ICS architecture, so these short definitions overlap rather than define mutually exclusive system families. The longer table supplies distributed-versus-local context; it does not rewrite generated clues.'],
 'section:ot-iot-cyber-physical:0':['Categories overlap: SCADA/DCS/PLC can participate in ICS, and IoT devices can also be OT. The examples are typical roles, not a universal geographic taxonomy or proof of isolation.'],
 'section:ot-iot-cyber-physical:1':['Integrity/availability/safety may dominate a particular decision without making confidentiality irrelevant. Long-lived or unsupported devices do not justify permanent unreviewed risk acceptance.','Interim controls reduce exposure but do not prove equivalent safety or repaired vulnerabilities. Vendor/engineering ownership, testing and rollback remain necessary; the held Compensating Controls card is not resolved.'],
 'section:ot-iot-cyber-physical:2':['Current profile marks this section optional enrichment. Segmentation and an industrial DMZ are controls to design/test, not automatic prevention or an asserted executed ISA62443 architecture.','Prefer passive discovery where active probes could disrupt; not a universal prohibition on approved safe active scanning. Strong authentication, remote logging, manual/fail-safe procedures and time sync remain equipment/process-specific and unobserved.'],
 'section:ot-iot-cyber-physical:3':['These are acquisition/support expectations to evaluate in context, not a claim all constrained devices provide endpoint agents or every listed mechanism. Network controls do not magically add missing device capabilities.','Unique identity is not necessarily a secret credential. Lifecycle revocation/sanitization needs verification; no device is procured, patched, erased or destroyed.']
};
